# Rust build artifact
target

# Local git worktrees (`just worktree-new`)
.worktrees

# Model weights and other files fetched at test or bench time. They are
# third-party material under their own terms and are never committed; see
# PUBLIC_DEVELOPMENT.md, "Third-party material".
models

# What this repository tells an agent is AGENTS.md. Claude Code reads
# CLAUDE.md instead, so the one tracked file under .claude/ is a symlink back
# to AGENTS.md. Everything else a session leaves — a personal CLAUDE.local.md,
# a CLAUDE.md beside a crate, local settings — is somebody's local state.
# `CLAUDE*.md` matches at every depth; `**/.claude/*` is the directory itself.
# The negation goes last because git takes the last matching pattern.
CLAUDE*.md
**/.claude/*
!.claude/CLAUDE.md

# Python bytecode beside the sidecar scripts under scripts/. Running a script
# through `uv` can leave it, and a staged .pyc is a build artifact in the tree.
__pycache__/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
